**Verdict: ABSENT.** No primary source forces every affine-image map-dicritical of a Keller map to have generic local degree `μ ≥ 2`.

What the literature does give:

- `μ ≥ 1` on every map-dicritical, and an `N−1` budget (Orevkov Lemma 4.2 / Cor. 4.3; Chau 2011 covering).
- At least one ramified dicritical in a counterexample (Orevkov’s `N=2,3` covering argument; Borisov Thm 3.1).
- Named special cases only: all-unramified configurations; a unique component of multiplicity `N−1`; Lê 2008 for *function*-dicriticals of degree 1 on a simple rational polynomial.

The mixed profile that is the live bit — a ramified owner plus a separate `μ=1` dicritical with affine image — is not forbidden. Żołądek Prop. 6.7 is the literature form of the day’s `μ = 1 + v(dx∧dy)`: in an N–P chart, `μ=1` iff `l−k=1`. No fetched source excludes that under the Jacobian condition.

Successor attack routes and an exact acquisition list (Lê–Weber 1994 journal PDF, Abhyankar–Luengo, Abhyankar 2010, Domrina 2000, …) are in the report.
